WEBVTT

00:07:28.163 --> 00:07:30.246
I just rolled down the window
and gunned it.

00:07:30.246 --> 00:07:33.038
And I made it across
and I had the samples,

00:07:33.079 --> 00:07:35.788
which was a good thing
because there were some surprises.

00:07:35.788 --> 00:07:39.038
We did find soldiers
and people from Spain, probably Andalusia,

00:07:39.079 --> 00:07:40.538
where Columbus sailed from,

00:07:40.579 --> 00:07:42.621
and maybe other parts
of the Mediterranean.

00:07:42.663 --> 00:07:45.204
But we also found
an indigenous Taíno woman,

00:07:45.246 --> 00:07:46.496
a local one,

00:07:46.538 --> 00:07:48.913
and other women who came from Europe,

00:07:48.954 --> 00:07:50.204
and one person who,

00:07:50.246 --> 00:07:53.788
if we can get some DNA
to see if this is actually true,

00:07:53.829 --> 00:07:55.538
may have been from Africa.

00:07:55.579 --> 00:07:58.371
None of these people
were on the ships' rosters.

00:07:58.413 --> 00:08:01.538
Teeth can tell us things
that the history books leave out.